  "summary": "A woman in her 20s in Dubai presented with 7-day quotidian fever >39C, severe myalgia, pharyngitis, transient salmon rash, and antibiotic-refractory sepsis. Despite multiple prior antibiotics (ceftriaxone, ceftazidime/avibactam, ciprofloxacin, linezolid), no improvement. Labs: CRP 342 mg/L, WBC 22.2 (91% neutrophils), ferritin 1528 ng/mL, ESR 71. All microbiology negative. AOSD per Yamaguchi criteria. IV methylprednisolone pulse: rapid response (CRP 60, WBC 13 at day 7). Discharged on tapering prednisolone. Outpatient biochemical flare: ferritin 8807 ng/mL; tocilizumab + methotrexate + hydroxychloroquine added with excellent response at 2 weeks. No MAS/HLH at any point. Classic systemic AOSD."
}
